<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clan Sinclair</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clan Sinclair is a Scottish clan of Norman origin based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caithness">Caithness</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a>. In 1379 Henry Sinclair was invested as Earl of Orkney by the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, and his descendants held the earldom until William Sinclair gave it up to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-iii-of-scotland">James III of Scotland</a> in 1470. The family later held the earldom of Caithness and built Rosslyn Chapel.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clan-sinclair.jpg" alt="Clan Sinclair" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Celtus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clan_member_crest_badge_-_Clan_Sinclair.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
